    "Q-01":{correct:"a",feedback:{a:"Correct. The harness is the software around the model that provides context, memory, tools, state, execution, and feedback.",b:"An LLM does not retain prior interaction by itself.",c:"Memory works with the context window; it does not remove it.",d:"The harness is more than UI; it manages the agent runtime."}},
    "Q-02":{correct:"a",feedback:{a:"Correct. Procedural memory is knowing how the user prefers work done.",b:"Semantic memory is for durable facts, not a way of working.",c:"Episodic memory recalls events and timing.",d:"The example is a durable preference, not only current working context."}},
    "Q-03":{correct:["a","b","d"],feedback:{a:"Correct. Short-term context helps the current run.",b:"Correct. Long-term memory can persist across sessions and time.",c:"That describes conversational context, not the full long-term model.",d:"Correct. Those are the three long-term categories in the PowerUP model."}},
    "Q-04":{correct:"a",feedback:{a:"Correct. The write story combines assistant traces, activity signals, and consolidation.",b:"The PowerUP explicitly includes activity and implicit learnings, not only explicit chat commands.",c:"Activity complements traces; it does not replace them.",d:"The described architecture includes agents and a consolidation path."}},
    "Q-05":{correct:"a",feedback:{a:"Correct. Progressive disclosure balances relevance and token cost.",b:"Memory is not hidden; relevant memory is selectively loaded.",c:"The opposite is true: the whole archive is not loaded on every turn.",d:"The memory layer complements, not replaces, enterprise search."}},
    "Q-06":{correct:"a",feedback:{a:"Correct. Daily consolidation and deployment-specific availability are the caveats to state.",b:"That overpromises timing and parity.",c:"That misses the cross-surface direction described in the PowerUP.",d:"The product story includes user review, edit, and delete controls."}}
